  ["", "", "", "凡 jom", "", "41合"],
  ["曾", "登 ong", "", "蒸 ing", "", "42開"],
  ["", "登 wong", "", "(職) wik", "", "43合"],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="攝 and Rime Reference"
  description="Private reference tables for Middle Chinese rime classes."
  fullWidth
  noindex
>
  <p><a href="/tools/han-character/">Back to Han character lookup</a></p>
  <h1>攝 and Rime Reference</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Middle Chinese rime classes in Baxter-Sagart notation</p>
  <div class="description">
    <p>
      <span lang="ko">섭</span> <span lang="zh">攝</span> is a broad rime group. A single
      <span lang="zh">攝</span> contains several related rimes, usually connected by a similar
      main vowel and ending. For example, <span lang="zh">山攝</span> gathers rimes such as
      <span lang="zh">山</span>, <span lang="zh">元</span>, <span lang="zh">仙</span>, and
      <span lang="zh">先</span>; <span lang="zh">梗攝</span> gathers rimes such as
      <span lang="zh">庚</span>, <span lang="zh">耕</span>, <span lang="zh">清</span>, and
      <span lang="zh">青</span>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span lang="zh">轉</span> is the row class used here to place those rimes into a more specific
      rime-table position. It tracks the row’s openness or closedness together with the table
      position: for instance, the <span lang="zh">宕攝</span> rows distinguish
      <span lang="zh">31開</span> from <span lang="zh">32合</span>, while
      <span lang="zh">梗攝</span> distinguishes <span lang="zh">33開</span>,
      <span lang="zh">34合</span>, <span lang="zh">35開</span>, and
      <span lang="zh">36合</span>. The lookup page then combines rime, division, and closed-mouth
      status into compact labels.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="sheet">
    <h2 lang="ko">BS</h2>
    <div class="rime-table-wrapper">
      <table class="rime-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            {bsRows[0].map((cell) => (
              <th scope="col">{cell}</th>
            ))}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {bsRows.slice(1).map((row) => (
            <tr>
              {row.map((cell, cellIndex) => (
                cellIndex === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td>{cell}</td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-note">
      In the <span lang="zh">臻</span> and <span lang="zh">真</span> rimes,
      <span lang="zh">臻</span> combines with <span lang="zh">莊二組</span>, while
      <span lang="zh">真</span> combines with the remaining initials.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  p,
  .table-note,
  .rime-table {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .description {
    width: 55%;
  }

  .sheet {
    width: 55%;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .table-note {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--meta-color);
  }

  .rime-table-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    background: var(--bg-color);
  }

  .rime-table {
    width: max-content;
    min-width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .rime-table th,
  .rime-table td {
    min-width: 5rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--border-color) 62%, transparent);
    font-size: inherit;
    line-height: 1.45;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .rime-table thead th {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background: var(--bg-color);
  }

  .rime-table tbody th {
    position: sticky;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background: var(--bg-color);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .description,
    .sheet {
      max-width: 100%;
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
